      "title": "Issue list",
      "summary": "The list searches, filters, and runs actions on issues without loading the complete result set.",
      "html": "<h2>Who can perform the operation</h2>\n<p>Reading requires issue access; creation and bulk actions have separate permissions.</p>\n<h2>Where to find the feature</h2>\n<p>Choose Issues in Work management.</p>\n<h2>How to perform the operation</h2>\n<p>Select a scope and project, set filters, and apply them. Open an issue by its key. Select rows to use the available bulk actions.</p>\n<h2>Result</h2>\n<p>The table shows a server-side page with columns derived from the project's field profile.</p>\n<h2>Limitations and special cases</h2>\n<p>“Select all” covers the complete current filter, not only the visible page. A bulk job can report errors for individual items.</p>\n<h2>Related topics</h2>\n<p>See <a href=\"/task-management/documentation/issue-detail\">Issue details</a> and <a href=\"/task-management/documentation/projects\">Projects</a>.</p>\n",
