      "title": "Issue details",
      "summary": "The issue page combines description, state, fields, comments, activity, files, links, tags, and work time.",
      "html": "<h2>Who can perform the operation</h2>\n<p>Reading requires access to the issue's project. Editing, transitions, and content management require update permission.</p>\n<h2>Where to find the feature</h2>\n<p>Open a key from a list or board, or use a direct address ending with a key such as <code>issue/DEV-123</code>.</p>\n<h2>How to perform the operation</h2>\n<p>Edit individual values in their sections. Choose an allowed transition and complete any required-fields dialog. Add comments, attachments, and time entries in their sections.</p>\n<h2>Result</h2>\n<p>Each saved change refreshes the page and is represented in history or the activity stream.</p>\n<h2>Limitations and special cases</h2>\n<p>A missing transition means the workflow does not allow it. Links use the readable issue key rather than the technical UUID.</p>\n<h2>Related topics</h2>\n<p>Return to the <a href=\"/task-management/documentation/issues-list\">Issue list</a> or see the <a href=\"/task-management/documentation/board\">Board</a>.</p>\n",
