      "title": "Backlog and sprints",
      "summary": "The backlog plans issues into a sprint, starts an iteration, and resolves unfinished items when it closes.",
      "html": "<h2>Who can perform the operation</h2>\n<p>Access to the board's issues is required; sprint management follows project permissions.</p>\n<h2>Where to find the feature</h2>\n<p>Open a Scrum board and navigate to its Backlog page.</p>\n<h2>How to perform the operation</h2>\n<p>Create a sprint, drag issues between backlog and sprint, then start it. When closing, choose how unfinished cards should be handled.</p>\n<h2>Result</h2>\n<p>Issues preserve their rank and iteration assignment, and the board displays the active sprint.</p>\n<h2>Limitations and special cases</h2>\n<p>The backlog exists only in a specific board context. Conflicting iterations and project rule violations are rejected.</p>\n<h2>Related topics</h2>\n<p>See the <a href=\"/task-management/documentation/boards\">Board list</a> and <a href=\"/task-management/documentation/board\">Working on a board</a>.</p>\n",
